      "proof_strategy": "Use the second disjunct for return_wit_1 and the first disjunct for return_wit_2. For return_wit_1, substitute first = linklist_pre and destruct nodes_general; the nonempty xizi_dllseg branch contradicts its node <> stop guard, while the nil branch makes first_value definitionally 0 and preserves the identical segment. For return_wit_2, destruct nodes_general and unfold the precondition xizi_dllseg: the nil case contradicts first <> linklist_pre, while the cons case exposes first = expected, first <> NULL, first <> linklist_pre, the first-node links, and the recursive tail. Substitute expected and rebuild xizi_dll with the existing xizi_dll_nonempty_rev rule plus the sentinel links. For derive_nil_case_by_general, choose nodes_general = nil, frame/cancel xizi_dll linklist_pre nil, introduce the wand using apply_sepcon_adjoint, choose retval = 0, simplify first_value nil, and close the retained spatial resource plus equality directly.",
